    "https://www.depauw.edu/academics/honors-fellows-programs/": {
      "title": "Honor Scholar & Fellow Programs",
      "description": "Honor Scholars & Fellow Programs - DePauw University DePauw University Students Families Employees Alumni Search Academics Academics Develop the leadership skills, critical thinking and experience necessary to lead in today’s world. Our brilliant faculty and co-curricular liberal arts approach make this transformation possible. Discover More Majors & Minors College of Liberal Arts and Sciences The Creative School School of Business and Leadership The Institute of Music Honor Scholars & Fellow Programs Centers at DePauw Academic Resources Study Abroad Research Internships Outcomes Admission & Aid Admission & Aid Your college degree is a vital investment in your future. We partner with you and your family to ensure the accessibility of our extraordinary academic and residential programs. Discover More Apply Scholarships & Aid The DePauw Promise Plan Your Visit Contact Admission Admitted Students Campus Life Campus Life Experience college life in high definition on our very involved and interconnected campus. With over 100 clubs and organizations plus a continuous calendar of community activities, there is no shortage of opportunity to get involved. Discover More Activities and Organizations Performing Arts & Culture Diversity and Inclusion Living on Campus Spiritual Life Fraternity & Sorority Life Wellness Athletics About About DePauw Discover a transformative learning environment that empowers you to be influential; to make a tangible difference on a global scale. Here you won’t just earn an education, you’ll live it. Discover More Mission and Impact Initiatives President White Location History & Traditions Quick Facts Our Community Stories Capital Projects Button Menu Visit Apply Get Info Give Honor Scholar & Fellow Programs Academics Honor Scholars & Fellow Programs The most transformative leaders start as students granted a stage. This is yours. Honor Scholar Honor Scholar is DePauw's interdisciplinary honors program, open to students for any major. Scholars take interdisciplinary seminars across the arts, sciences, and social sciences. In their senior year, they write a self-designed thesis with a faculty committee they help choose. Discover More Media Fellows Media Fellows integrate four semesters at The DePauw newspaper, WGRE radio , or D3 Network , with a professional internship and a senior capstone. Students get hands-on studio experience, land off-campus internships, and meet media professionals through a regular speaker series. Discover More Management Fellows More than 1,000 graduates of DePauw's Management Fellows graduates now work in finance, consulting, and leadership roles worldwide. The program pairs eight core credits, including a full-time internship, with one elective and a senior seminar, building business skills on top of a liberal arts foundation. Discover More Environmental Fellows Environmental Fellows follows a four-year plan: a first-year seminar, six courses across the natural and social sciences, a practicum, and a senior capstone. Open to any major, it trains problem-solvers to tackle climate change, pollution, biodiversity loss and environmental justice. Discover More Science Research Fellows Science Research Fellows is a four-year research track for science majors. Students write proposals, do science coursework, participate in an eight to ten week research experience supported by two professional skills courses, and enjoy close faculty mentorship. Discover More Global Studies Fellows Global Studies Fellows adds a global lens to any major. Students complete two core courses in a thematic track, two in a regional track, language study, a global experience abroad or at home, and a capstone – plus paid leadership opportunities and two Global Insight events per semester. Discover More Information Technology Associates Program (ITAP) ITAP is a paid, year-long, on-campus internship, open to any major with no work-study required. Students work on real technology projects alongside faculty and staff, build professional and leadership skills without leaving campus. Discover More Request Information Loading... DePauw University DePauw University 204 E. Seminary Greencastle, Indiana 46135-0037 Phone (765) 658-4800 Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Athletics About Strategic Plan Directories Library Events News Employment Moodle Workday Google Apps Schedule a visit © 2026 DePauw University. All rights reserved.  DePauw University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. It does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Terms and Conditions | Notice at Collection | Your Privacy Choices | Non-Discrimination Policy | Title IX"
