ositions Founded in 1837, DePauw University is a selective, undergraduate, national liberal arts college of just over 1,900 students, with a separate Institute of Music . The University, which has an endowment of $730 million, is located in Greencastle, Indiana, a town of 10,000 people, within an hour’s drive of Indianapolis, Terre Haute and Bloomington. Among DePauw’s distinctive features are its innovative Honors and Fellows programs , a strong tradition of community service, a large internship program, numerous international education programs , and success in attracting a diverse student body. DePauw has exceptional programs for supporting its faculty , including pre-tenure leaves for new faculty members and short- and long-term internal funding for professional and curriculum development activities. In support of DePauw University's mission and values, we welcome applications from members of underrepresented groups. DePauw University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, age, or veteran status or any other federal, state, or local protected class. Faculty Positions Department Position Status Field/Specialty Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Bassoon Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Clarinet Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Dance Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Music Education Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Violin Review of applications will begin on the indicated date and continue until positions are filled. For further information about these positions, write to the chair or dean of the corresponding department or school. Visit the Human Resources website for more information on other employment opportunities and job benefits at DePauw. Access DePauw University's Annual Safety Report here . Institute of MusicPart-Time Assistant ProfessorAccepting Applications DePauw University DePauw University 204 E. Seminary Greencastle, Indiana 46135-0037 Phone (765) 658-4800 Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Athletics About Strategic Plan Directories Library Events News Employment Moodle Workday Google Apps Schedule a visit © 2026 DePauw University. All rights reserved.  DePauw University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. It does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Terms and Conditions | Notice at Collection | Your Privacy Choices | Non-Discrimination Policy | Title IX"
